    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.completion, mini.pairs\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nHi! So in nvim-autopairs, there is this functionality where in after a item is completed from completion menu based on its type like if the entry is a function, a parenthesis is added automatically by nvim-autopairs using this code\r\n```lua\r\nlocal cmp_autopairs = require('nvim-autopairs.completion.cmp')\r\nlocal cmp = require('cmp')\r\ncmp.event:on(\r\n  'confirm_done',\r\n  cmp_autopairs.on_confirm_done()\r\n)\r\n```\r\nIs there any mechanism as such available for mini.pairs with mini.completion. If not are there any plans to implement such feature.",
